From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] activities of another package start in that package's own process

Context.startActivity() and Activity.startActivityForResult() created
every activity inside the calling process, also one whose component names
another package: its classes are not there (ClassNotFoundException), and
since other packages' code is no longer loaded into the caller, "Open" in
an application store did nothing.

An intent whose component or package names another installed package is
now handed to that package (ATLExternalStart): the caller checks that the
package is installed, the activity exists, is enabled and exported
(ActivityNotFoundException otherwise) and that the caller holds the
permission the activity asks for (SecurityException); then the session
bus is asked to start the package's process if it is not running and the
request goes to its "startActivity" action, with action, component, data
and the extras that can be carried (strings, parcelables). A package the
bus cannot start is started with `--package` directly. On the target's
side the request is checked again, the application is brought in front
(a process started for it gets its window and main activity now), and an
activity other than the launcher one is put on top.

A result cannot travel back from the other process yet:
startActivityForResult() starts the activity and reports RESULT_CANCELED
at once instead of leaving the caller waiting.

ActivityNotFoundException is a RuntimeException with a message, as on
Android (it was a checked exception without constructors).

Callbacks that GTK calls for clicks, touches, hover and scrolling clear an
exception the application threw after reporting it; left pending it
aborted the process at the next JNI call. Hover callbacks without a
current event (GTK makes up a crossing when a widget appears under the
pointer) no longer ask it for a position.

